The serial devices crosvm emulates as the kernel's serial console: the SBSA UART (a PL011 subset, xnu-12377's own PL011_UART
driver, "arm,pl011") and a 16550 COM port (a new NS16550_UART driver, "ns16550a": byte registers one byte apart, polled). xnu-12377
takes the one device a phandle names: the ADT's /defaults serial-device, the boot-arg serial-device-name=NODE, and here
/defaults droidvm,serial-device as well, which DarwinBoot sets to the VM's console UART (FdtAdt.c) under a name only this kernel
reads -- the standard property naming a UART an unpatched kernel has no driver for panics it before its console. serial=3 is built
in (DroidVMBootArgs27.c): output and the serial keyboard (the 16 ms poll feeding /dev/console); a VM without a console UART
clears it, so it runs as before and polls nothing.

The fileset matcher paired the original kernel's PAGE_SHIFT_CONST with cons_ops_index once this code referenced it (APFS then
paged in with a page shift of 0 or 1): ipados27/fileset-reviewed.json holds the pairing.

